      <p class="c1"><span class="c13"></span></p>
      <ol class="c5 lst-kix_list_26-0 start" start="1">
         <li class="c8 c28 li-bullet-2"><span class="c2">After ICRA has informed your Company of the Rating it has assigned, your Company shall communicate its decision to ICRA regarding its acceptance of the Rating in writing, and intended use of the Rating, in any manner, within 5 (five) working days of the assignment of the Rating. In the event your Company fails to notify ICRA of its decision regarding its acceptance/non-acceptance of the Rating or failed to appeal against the Rating during such 5 (five) working days acceptance time period, such failure shall be treated by ICRA as non-acceptance of the Rating and the Rating shall be disclosed by ICRA on its website, within 30 (thirty) days of communication of Rating by ICRA, as unaccepted Rating. Any use by you of the Rating shall be deemed acceptance of the Rating. Also, in case any rating of the Security is published or otherwise disseminated by any other rating agency at any stage, or any other circumstances that ICRA may deem fit, ICRA will reserve the right to publish the Rating within a reasonable period of time.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="c1 c17"><span class="c2"></span></p>
      <ol class="c5 lst-kix_list_26-0" start="2">
         <li class="c8 c28 li-bullet-2" id="h.1fob9te"><span class="c20">During such 5 (five) working days as mentioned in Clause D (I), the Rating shall remain confidential subject to the terms of this Agreement, including without limitation, clause N </span><span class="c20 c23">(Applicant Confidentiality for Unpublished ratings). </span><span class="c2">On request, an unaccepted Rating may be converted to an accepted Rating, provided such request is made by your Company within 2 (two) months from the date ICRA first communicated its Rating decision to you. However, before such conversion is made, the Rating initially assigned may have to undergo a revalidation process. No additional fee would be charged to your Company for the conversion, unless the Rating initially assigned needs to undergo a revalidation process. The Rating initially assigned needs to undergo a revalidation process if either (i) the size of the Security or structure of the Security has changed before the Rating has been accepted by your Company, provided the revised size should not exceed the Security (which would constitute an enhancement not covered by or under this Agreement), or (ii) the request for conversion is received by ICRA after 2 (two) months from the date that ICRA first communicated its Rating decision to you. </span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="c1 c17"><span class="c2"></span></p>
      <ol class="c5 lst-kix_list_26-0" start="3">
         <li class="c8 c28 li-bullet-3"><span class="c2">In case a Rating is not accepted by your Company, or in case of failure of your Company to notify its acceptance or non-acceptance, as the case may be, the assigned Rating shall not be subject to surveillance and ICRA shall not be responsible for the continuous monitoring/surveillance of the assigned Rating.</span></li>
